After my run at the track today, I went to the grocery store to pick up apples, hummus and some other particulars. While in line for the check out, I saw that I had made a reminder to research "[transistors]{a type of semiconductor device that is used to conduct and insulate electric current or voltage.}" when I had a chance. It was weird to see that next to New Seasons shipping list, but I digress. 

Apparently, its deemed one of the best inventions in the history of science and engineering (according to Geeks for Geeks). Their are three layers of semiconductor material or terminals which helps to make a connection to any external circuit and all the layers do carry the current.

There are three terminals for transistors:
[Base]{To activate the transistor}
[Collector]{Positive lead of transistor}
[Emitter]{Negative lead of transistor}
